# Full Example: Feature Flags with User Context in Next.js App Router

Based on the documentation provided, here's how to implement feature flags with user identification:

## Define Your Flag

```tsx
// flags.ts
import { flag } from 'flags/next';

export const premiumFeature = flag({
  key: 'premium-feature',
  decide(context) {
    // Use context to make decisions based on user properties
    return context.userId && context.userTier === 'premium';
  },
});
```

## Use in App Router with User Context

```tsx
// app/page.tsx
import { premiumFeature } from '../flags';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';

export default async function Page() {
  // Build evaluation context from current user
  const userId = getUserId(); // Your auth logic
  const userTier = getUserTier(); // Your user data

  const showPremium = await premiumFeature({
    userId,
    userTier,
  });

  if (!showPremium) {
    redirect('/upgrade');
  }

  return <div>Premium content here</div>;
}
```

## Key Points

The Flags SDK enables you to "call the flag function from a page, component, or middleware to evaluate the flag." Pass user properties through the context object to make flag decisions based on individual user attributes rather than random evaluation.

